  "dom_id": "step-q35792",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ and $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$ be bases of ${R}^{2}.$ If ${b}_{1}=2{c}_{1}-7{c}_{2}$ and ${b}_{2}=4{c}_{2}-3{c}_{1},$ find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to C}$ from $B$ to $C.$",
  "worked_solution": "The coordinates of the vectors in $B$ relative to the basis $C$ are\n\n$$\n[{b}_{1}]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}],\\,[{b}_{2}]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $C.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -7 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
